<p>Porting over some <a href="/chat-guide">IRC chat</a> crit I provided.</p>
<hr />
<p>I think that this could be a really fun thing to play with. There's plenty of stuff working to its benefit: it's a simple object that does a simple thing. I personally advise cutting (heh) some of the extra bits like the visual hallucinations and the screeching, since that doesn't ever come up in your narrative here.</p>
<p>And while we're going that direction, I think the narrative is remarkably close to being solid. With the object being pretty innocuous (I'm personally imagining a small squid toy or a squid shaped sponge; a common bathroom object), it could lead people into a false sense of safety that would lend to that same fear of being cut on accident. The &quot;mush&quot; in the bathroom sink leaves a lot to the imagination and makes for some great fridge horror. Honestly, the whole thing could be done super well short, sweet, and scary.</p>
<p>I'm going to provide a conditional <strong><span style="color: green">greenlight</span></strong> here. As long as you shape the narrative a bit and lean into the aspects that we talked about, I think this could really do well as a short work. You do need two greenlights if you want to use the drafts forum, so I suggest reaching out to another reviewer.</p>

