<p>Alright, let's consider these in order.</p>
<ol>
<li>I'm not so sure how much this would solve your ambiguity problem. It still doesn't explain the disparity between your description of the object and its potential effects.</li>
<li>How would that resolve the story? You'd still have those two missing people, and I don't see how that ability would quite make sense when combined with the anomaly's existing qualities.</li>
<li>That could hypothetically work, but it would need a rehashing of the story to make the goo a more central aspect, in my view. I'm also not seeing a thematic connection between the core anomaly and the goo.</li>
<li>There are certainly ways to incorporate it. The narrative just needs to be tweaked to utilize it properly.</li>
</ol>

